
kubectl --> Realiza a criação/ler/atualizar/remover os componentes do cluster

kubectl apply -f app.yaml --> Inicia uma aplicação, onde vamos aplicar a configuração

kubectl get --> usado no Kubernetes para listar recursos do cluster
  pods --> Listar Pods --- kubectl get pods / kubectl get po
    kubectl get pods -o wide --> Mostrar IP e Node
    kubectl get pods -n producao --> Ver em namespace específico
    kubectl get pods -w --> Monitorar em tempo real
    kubectl get pods --show-labels --> Mostrar labels
    kubectl get pods --sort-by=.metadata.name --> Ordenar
    kubectl get pod nginx --> Apenas um Pod
    kubectl get pod nginx -o yaml --> Exportar em YAML
    kubectl get pod nginx -o json --> Exportar em JSON
  nodes --> Listar Nodes --- kubectl get nodes / kubectl get no
  svc --> Listar Services --- kubectl get svc / kubectl get services
  deployments --> Listar Deployments --- kubectl get deployments / kubectl get deploy
  namespaces --> Listar Namespaces --- kubectl get namespaces
  all --> Ver tudo do namespace (Pods, Services, Deployments, ReplicaSets) --- kubectl get all


